It did not have praying or artifacts.  In fact, it did not have very much.
Off the top of my head (and the differences are so numerous that I can
only remember scant percent of the total) there were only 6 classes: Knight,
Caveman, Tourist, Speciologist, Wizard, Fighter.  Only 56 monster types,
no fountains or statues or spellbooks.  No Kops, no cursed/blessed status,
there was a Hell (1 level) that you could get to by going below level 30,
there was a Heavan to levitate up to (I forget how), no branches, no temples,
the only stats were HP/HP_Max, Strength, and Armour Class.  The best weapon
in the games was a Crysknife, and the best armour was Plate Mail.  There was
no polypiling (oyu could only polymorph monsters, not objects) and to my
knowledge, Elbereth did not exist (I might be wrong on that one: it is listed
as a rumor though).  There were only a few intrinsics like telepathy (no
blind folds though), resist fire/poison/cold.  And the game was VERY VERY
hard.  Basically everything had to work out just right or you would run
into an "instadeath".  No one here at UCI in 8+ years of playing has ascended
in that version.

